{"concepto": "Generación paralela (Parallel generation)", "enunciado": "Diffusion language models generate text in arbitrary order and can generate multiple tokens simultaneously, bypassing the sequential constraint of autoregressive models", "problema": "Overcome the sequential bottleneck where N tokens require N forward passes in AR models", "limite": "Early diffusion models had lower quality than AR; quality improves with more steps", "patron": "A decoding procedure that can propose multiple output positions at once and refine them iteratively, starting from maximum uncertainty", "linea": 99}
{"concepto": "Proceso adelante por enmascaramiento (Forward masking process)", "enunciado": "q(z_t^(i) | x^(i)) = α_t if z_t^(i) = x^(i), 1-α_t if z_t^(i) = M, where each position independently masks with probability 1-α_t", "problema": "Establish a known forward corruption process with analytically tractable posterior for learning its reverse", "limite": "Assumes position-wise independence; α_t must be a scalar parameter", "patron": "Independent binary masking controlled by a scheduling parameter that interpolates between fully clean and fully masked states", "linea": 166}
{"concepto": "Posterior inverso (Reverse posterior)", "enunciado": "For masked positions: P(z_s^(i) = x^(i) | z_t^(i) = M, x^(i)) = (α_s - α_t)/(1-α_t); revealed positions unchanged", "problema": "Define exact transition probabilities for the denoising process given noisy observations", "limite": "Requires knowledge of true clean text x; appears only as theoretical oracle", "patron": "A closed-form Bayesian posterior derived from Bayes rule that specifies exact unmasking probabilities based on signal level changes", "linea": 185}
{"concepto": "Cota inferior de evidencia ponderada (Weighted ELBO)", "enunciado": "L_MDLM = E_{t~U(0,1), z_t~q(·|x)} [α_t'/(1-α_t) Σ_{i: z_t^(i)=M} -log x_θ^(i)(z_t, t)]", "problema": "Enable tractable training of discrete diffusion models without computing sequence likelihood", "limite": "Loss computed only at masked positions; weighting by unmasking probability", "patron": "A variational lower bound weighted by the derivative of signal level relative to noise, concentrating gradient on most informative timesteps", "linea": 221}
{"concepto": "Mecanismo de copia (Copy-over mechanism)", "enunciado": "For already-revealed positions, the Transformer outputs directly equal the inputs without modification; loss only on masked positions", "problema": "Simplify training by eliminating gradient computation on already-determined tokens", "limite": "Requires architectural support for copying; does not improve quality directly", "patron": "An identity-like operator that propagates known values unchanged while only computing predictions for unknowns", "linea": 205}
{"concepto": "Almacenamiento clave-valor (KV Caching)", "enunciado": "Cache frozen Key and Value activations from previous decoding steps to avoid recomputation when sequence grows incrementally", "problema": "Reduce per-step computation cost in sequential generation", "limite": "Only compatible with causal attention; activations must be immutable to cache safely", "patron": "Memoization of attention subcomputations based on the assumption that past activations do not change", "linea": 352}
{"concepto": "Tipo de mecanismo de atención (Attention mechanism type)", "enunciado": "Causal attention: each position depends only on left context; bidirectional attention: each position depends on entire context", "problema": "Trade off global context awareness against computability of KV cache", "limite": "Causal prevents true parallel generation; bidirectional prevents activation caching", "patron": "A masking operation on pairwise attention scores that enforces which positions can communicate, creating temporal or structural constraints", "linea": 140}
{"concepto": "Reordenamiento basado en ordenamiento (Sorting-based reordering)", "enunciado": "At each step, rearrange sequence to place unmasked tokens on left, masked tokens on right, then apply causal attention on reordered positions", "problema": "Enable KV caching in parallel diffusion models by converting bidirectional dependencies into causal form", "limite": "Requires dynamic permutation each step; changes effective position embeddings", "patron": "Permute input to create artificial causality where known values precede unknowns, enabling cached computation without losing global modeling", "linea": 396}
{"concepto": "Muestreo ancestral (Ancestral sampling)", "enunciado": "Initialize with full mask; loop: predict distributions for all masked positions, sample from distributions, keep fraction according to unmasking probability, remask others; repeat T times until all revealed", "problema": "Generate samples from a trained diffusion model while respecting the learned reverse process", "limite": "Quality degrades with fewer steps; different orderings of unmasking affect correlation structure", "patron": "Iterative refinement where each step proposes completions for all unknowns and probabilistically commits only to a stochastic subset", "linea": 263}
{"concepto": "Nivel de señal (Signal level)", "enunciado": "α_t ∈ [0,1] controls corruption amount: α_t=1 corresponds to clean text, α_t=0 corresponds to fully masked sequence", "problema": "Parametrize the noise schedule in continuous-time diffusion models", "limite": "Usually defined as monotone decreasing function; linear schedule shown in examples", "patron": "A scalar parameter that interpolates between boundary conditions (pristine and maximally corrupted states) over a single dimension", "linea": 152}
{"concepto": "Probabilidad de desmascaramiento (Unmasking probability)", "enunciado": "P(unmasking mask at position i in step s|t) = (α_s - α_t)/(1-α_t)", "problema": "Determine the fraction of masked tokens to reveal per denoising step", "limite": "Must have α_s > α_t; depends on schedule and timestep selection", "patron": "Rate-of-change weighting that normalizes signal change by current noise level, adapting reveal rate to corruption state", "linea": 270}
{"concepto": "Perplejidad (Perplexity)", "enunciado": "Standard language modeling metric measuring average bits needed per token; exponentiated cross-entropy loss on held-out data", "problema": "Quantitatively measure language model quality and compare models on same benchmark", "limite": "Correlates with downstream performance but metric depends on data distribution; not directly comparable across datasets", "patron": "A scalar summary statistic derived from negative log-likelihood that concentrates on common errors", "linea": 295}
{"concepto": "Límite de tiempo continuo (Continuous-time ELBO limit)", "enunciado": "As number of diffusion steps T → ∞, discrete Markov chain converges to continuous-time formulation; ELBO simplifies to the formula at line 221", "problema": "Simplify discrete diffusion theory by taking continuous limit for analytical tractability", "limite": "Approximation quality improves with larger T; requires differentiability assumptions on α_t schedule", "patron": "Replacing discrete summations with continuous integrals to obtain closed-form expressions with cleaner mathematical structure", "linea": 232}
{"concepto": "Frontera de Pareto (Pareto frontier)", "enunciado": "Set of solutions where no objective can be improved without worsening another; in generation, the curve of achievable (speed, quality) pairs", "problema": "Characterize fundamental, non-dominated trade-offs between conflicting optimization goals", "limite": "Achievable frontier depends on algorithm and implementation efficiency; may shift with hardware or algorithmic improvements", "patron": "A curve or surface in multi-dimensional objective space where improvement in one dimension necessitates sacrifice in another", "linea": 327}
{"concepto": "Sesgo izquierda-derecha en datos (Left-to-right bias in data)", "enunciado": "Natural language has inherent temporal ordering from left to right; other discrete data structures (proteins, molecules) have no such directional bias", "problema": "Explain performance differences: why AR models excel at text but diffusion may excel at non-sequential discrete data", "limite": "Only applies to structured sequential data with directional information", "patron": "An inductive bias in data geometry that makes sequential generation easier than unordered generation for that domain", "linea": 324}
{"concepto": "Difusión por bloques (Block-wise diffusion)", "enunciado": "Split sequence into fixed-size blocks; apply masked diffusion within each block; use autoregressive generation across block boundaries", "problema": "Enable partial KV caching in diffusion models by limiting bidirectional attention to block scope", "limite": "Quality degrades significantly when reducing diffusion steps per block; block boundaries create artificial constraints", "patron": "A hybrid approach layering local parallel generation with global sequential generation to achieve intermediate speed-quality tradeoff", "linea": 454}
